title: Birth of a Party
tags: event
view-if: year = 1932 and month = 5
priority: 2
max-visits: 1

In Calgary, a meeting is set to be held, consisting of various labour, farmer, and socialist organizations to discuss the formation of a new Dominion-wide movement dedicated to social and economic planning. 

- @attend_ccf_formation: We send delegates representing the UFC(SS) and the Saskatchewan ILP

@attend_ccf_formation 
face-image: img/portraits/ccf_founding.jpg

= The New Face of Socialism

The meeting is fruitful. Representatives from the: 

Socialist Party of Canada

United Farmers of Alberta

Dominion Labor Party

Canadian Labour Party

United Farmers of Canada (Saskatchewan Section)

Independent Labour Party

Canadian Brotherhood of Railway Employees

